  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ukraine Humanitarian Response and Early Recovery 2025-2026 (FCDO III)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In response to continued humanitarian needs and consequent impact of the conflict in Ukraine, this project will build upon the Ukrainian Red Cross Society (URCS) activities funded by FCDO from 2023 to 2025 and BRC bilateral funding. Expressed through a new FCDO MoU, funding will support the URCS emergency response and disaster management capacities as well as their medium to long-term ambitions as expressed through their &#x2018;One Plan&#x2019;.
 
In alignment with BRC and URCS strategies, the FCDO 25/26 project has been designed in close collaboration with URCS, with all activities aligned with the URCS One Plan. BRC has a wider programmatic engagement with URCS that is supported by bilateral funding from its Ukraine Appeal. Activities within this programme will support elements of this project.

FCDO III 2025-26 is a key component of the BRC-URCS programme and is viewed as a step towards a longer-term funding relationship that will ensure the sustainability of URCS over the next three to five years. This project therefore seeks to balance investment in immediate humanitarian needs with activities that underpin the capacity and strategic ambitions of the URCS and contribute to greater resilience and early recovery.

In response to learnings from 2023 to present, this project has been designed to include more effective targeting of activities, aligned with a more focused technical approach and ability to show outcomes.  Cash assistance will be a key modality to achieving objectives involving relief and recovery efforts, and a main cost driver amounting to approximately 40% of the project budget.</narrative>
  </description>
